tude scores; SME review required."}, "big5_assessment": {"traits": ["Conscientiousness", "Emotional Stability", "Agreeableness"], "rationale": "Disciplined checks and sound escalation support decisions without crossing procurement authority boundaries. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria."}, "work_values_assessment": {"values": ["Security", "Impact", "Financial Growth"], "rationale": "Transparent use of resources and financial control are meaningful; no compensation outcome is implied. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees."}}, "embedding_text": "ROLE\nName: Water Project Finance & Procurement Associate\n\nCAREER CONTEXT\nIndustry: Water Resources, Environment and Public Utilities\nDomain: Water Project Finance and Procurement\nRole Family: Water Project Financial Controls\n\nROLE SUMMARY\nWater Project Finance & Procurement Associate supports control resources and expenditure in the RAREMINDS River Mission workplace case. May prepare financial analyses and recommendations; cannot approve a supplier, place a purchase order, authorise payment or treat conditional scope as spending approval.\n\nWORK CONTEXT\nL4 option costing, quote evaluation, procurement control → L5 finance-route portfolio. Inputs: vendor rates and technical eligibility documents, budget quantity/rate lines, APP-03 decision and ledger statuses. Course-wide foundations: CAP01, CAP02, CAP06, CAP07, CAP08, CAP11. Role focus: CAP09, CAP10. May prepare financial analyses and recommendations; cannot approve a supplier, place a purchase order, authorise payment or treat conditional scope as spending approval. Support-only degree pathways listed in source: B.Com.\n\nTYPICAL WORK ACTIVITIES\nWater Project Finance & Procurement Associate: Compare three vendor quotes including quantity, transport and technical evidence; Build the five-line quantity × rate project budget; Separate proposed, conditional, committed, invoiced and paid amounts; Record procurement exceptions and approval dependencies. When source evidence is missing, record a HOLD/exception and identify the reviewing owner.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACTIONS\nCompare three vendor quotes including quantity, transport and technical evidence; Build the five-line quantity × rate project budget; Separate proposed, conditional, committed, invoiced and paid amounts; Record procurement exceptions and approval dependencies; Check each saved record against source ID, units, errors and role authority.\n\nDELIVERABLES & OUTPUTS\nSource-backed outputs: Vendor quotation and technical eligibility matrix; Calculated budget and ceiling comparison; Approval/commitment/expenditure ledger; Finance and procurement exception handover. Associated capability evidence: CAP01 Investigation brief; CAP02 Stakeholder and site register; CAP06 Validated analytical workbook; CAP07 Evidence and hypothesis matrix; CAP08 Criteria comparison and gap report; CAP09 Option evaluation model; CAP10 Project action pack; CAP11 Final professional investigation portfolio.\n\nINTEREST AND WORK-STYLE ALIGNMENT\nCEI (Conventional/Enterprising/Investigative): C supports controlled transaction evidence; E supports commercial comparison and vendor coordination; I supports eligibility checks and variance analysis. Proposed role-environment orientation, not an individual assessment.\n\nAPTITUDE ALIGNMENT\nKey areas: Numerical Reasoning, Data Interpretation, Logical Reasoning\nReadiness: Accurate rates, budgets, approval states and invoice checks require strong numerical and reconciliation skills. These are draft importance estimates for role requirements, not learner aptitude scores; SME review required.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL ALIGNMENT\nKey traits: Conscientiousness, Emotional Stability, Agreeableness\nWork style: Disciplined checks and sound escalation support decisions without crossing procurement authority boundaries. Trait-demand ratings are provisional role descriptors, not personality diagnosis or exclusion criteria.\n\nWORK-VALUE ALIGNMENT\nKey values: Security, Impact, Financial Growth\nMotivation: Transparent use of resources and financial control are meaningful; no compensation outcome is implied. Work-value ratings are provisional career-exploration descriptors, not employment or pay guarantees.\n\nEDUCATION AND ELIGIBILITY\nGate: Preferred\nStreams: B.Com; BBA; MBA Operations; MBA Finance; MBA Sustainability; BA Economics\n"}'::jsonb;
